\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.2}{\ignorespaces Statistics of the controlled 3D pendulum for desired rotations about the $x$-axis. The terminal error is defined as $e_R(T)=\lVert R_N-R_{\mathrm  {des}}\rVert _F$. The manifold violation is $\max _k\varepsilon _{R,k}$ with $\varepsilon _{R,k}=\lVert R_k^\top R_k-I_3\rVert _F$. The rank metric $\delta _{\max }$ follows Teng's definition $\delta _k=|\lambda _{k,2}|/|\lambda _{k,1}|$, computed over the actual sub-moment matrices used for trajectory extraction. The trajectory quantities are evaluated using the ordered extraction, and the reported runtime is the MOSEK optimizer time.}}{78}{table.caption.62}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:pendulum_3d_sdp_statistics}{{6.2}{78}{Statistics of the controlled 3D pendulum for desired rotations about the $x$-axis. The terminal error is defined as $e_R(T)=\lVert R_N-R_{\mathrm {des}}\rVert _F$. The manifold violation is $\max _k\varepsilon _{R,k}$ with $\varepsilon _{R,k}=\lVert R_k^\top R_k-I_3\rVert _F$. The rank metric $\delta _{\max }$ follows Teng's definition $\delta _k=|\lambda _{k,2}|/|\lambda _{k,1}|$, computed over the actual sub-moment matrices used for trajectory extraction. The trajectory quantities are evaluated using the ordered extraction, and the reported runtime is the MOSEK optimizer time}{table.caption.62}{}}
